## Description 

The top-level commit of a stack of PRs for ensuring that a `GraphQL` query is consistent from its root to leaf. To do so, we thread a `checkpoint_viewed_at: Option<u64>` field through each `GraphQL` type. This field is populated when a type is resolved and when a cursor is built. This field needs to be on cursors as well, so that when paginating through a connection, we can lock the pagination queries to a specific checkpoint in time.

A few queries to demonstrate:
```
{
  transactionBlock(digest:"digest"){
    sender {
      objects {
        nodes {
          address, version
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
The query is made at checkpoint 10, thus `checkpoint_viewed_at=10`. The nested `objects` field inherits `checkpoint_viewed_at=10`.

```
{
  object(address: "address", version: 10) {
    owner {
      ... on AddressOwner {
        owner {
          objects {
            nodes {
              digest
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Similarly, the nested owner and objects all inherit `checkpoint_viewed_at=10`.

```
query {
  address(address: "...") {
    coins(type: "0x2::sui::SUI") {
      nodes { 
        owner {
          ... on AddressOwner {
            owner { asAddress { balance(type: "0x2::sui::SUI") { totalBalance } } }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
If `checkpoint_viewed_at=10`, then each coin result will yield an owner that inherits `checkpoint_viewed_at=10`. Subsequently, each balance result reflects the owner's balance at checkpoint 10.

```
query {
  address(address: "...") {
    coins(type: "0x2::sui::SUI", cursor:"checkpoint=10") {
      nodes { 
        owner {
          ... on AddressOwner {
            owner { asAddress { balance(type: "0x2::sui::SUI") { totalBalance } } }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Some time later, the user makes another query using a cursor from the first query. Now, `checkpoint_viewed_at=20`. When we hit the coins connection field, `checkpoint_viewed_at` is set to `10`, and this value is inherited by the rest of the children.



